---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
import { COMMERCE_ENABLED } from '../lib/launch-config';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Shop Terms"
  description="The terms that apply to orders placed through the Cloud Peptides shop."
  lastUpdated="August 8, 2026"
>
  {
    !COMMERCE_ENABLED && (
      <p class="cp-policy-note">
        <strong>Ordering is not currently enabled on this site.</strong> The shop catalog is visible
        as a preview only — nothing can be added to a cart or purchased right now. The terms below
        describe what will apply once ordering opens.
      </p>
    )
  }

  <h2>Research use only</h2>
  <p>
    Everything in our shop is sold for laboratory research use only and is not for human
    consumption. No claims of safety or effectiveness for human use are made or implied. See our
    full <a href="/disclaimer">Research and Medical Disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Eligibility</h2>
  <p>You must be at least 18 years old to place an order.</p>

  <h2>Legal status is your responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    Laws governing research chemicals and peptides vary by location. It is your responsibility to
    know and follow the laws that apply to you before ordering.
  </p>

  <h2>Payment</h2>
  <p>
    This site does not collect or process payment card data directly. When ordering is enabled, an
    order request records the payment method you select (for example, cryptocurrency, Zelle, or
    PayPal), and payment itself is arranged directly between you and us through that method, outside
    this website's systems.
  </p>

  <h2>Batch testing</h2>
  <p>
    We intend to make batch testing documentation available for applicable products once ordering is
    enabled. Batch testing/COA documentation is a commerce record, not scientific evidence — it's
    kept separate from, and is never cited within, our published research claims.
  </p>

  <h2>Pricing and availability</h2>
  <p>
    Prices and product availability shown in the shop are subject to change and are not a binding
    offer until an order is actually placed once ordering is enabled.
  </p>

  <h2>Shipping and returns</h2>
  <p>
    See our <a href="/shipping">Shipping Policy</a> and
    <a href="/returns">Return and Refund Policy</a> — both will be finalized before ordering opens.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/contact">Contact us</a> with any question about an order or these terms.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
